# `pkill` and `killall -r` search their expression in each name; a plain word
# is compared whole by `killall`, and `-x` wants the whole name. A pattern
# that can match every process or a system name is `stop_system`.
posix safe | killall login
posix safe | killall Window
posix safe | killall launch
# `pkill -f server` is not in `WindowServer` (the case counts).
posix safe | pkill -x login
posix safe | pkill -x '^login$'
posix safe | pkill -f server
