# A line is signal 0 only when the first word after `kill` is exactly `-0`,
# `-s 0`, `-n 0` or `--signal=0`, and every later word is a literal positive
# id, a job, `$!`, `$$`, `$PPID` or a plain variable. Otherwise the shell and
# the `kill` program may still send a real signal, and the ids are judged.
